From 63b4f83cbeebefe3e878f4bd8c59298da9200804 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul <paulsleepm@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 04:21:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(agent): when the run says a limit cannot be checked yet,
 the Agent suggests no step to make it checkable

One sentence after the fragile/near-tie rule in AGENT_INSTRUCTIONS (both the Agent's own call and the
explicit Run's interpreting call). Measured on 8 served e39f6e0 Run inputs carrying #1875's honest copy,
n=2, blind OpenAI labeller: replies inviting a step to make the limit checkable 4/16 -> 0/16; 16/16 still
say the limit was unchecked. Contrast (legitimate root repair): relays 4/16 -> 2/16, other-fix 3/16 -> 4/16,
within noise. Pinned on the sent instructions; RED without the clause (2/2).

Supersedes #1872 (its relay sentence assumed a repair the honest copy no longer names).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
